# A shy, awkward suitor: he fumbles his words, gets a compliment wrong, apologises too much and
# finally asks her out badly but sincerely. Lena should find it endearing: amusement, warmth,
# attraction and a little embarrassment, teasing kindly rather than brushing him off.
# speaker | what the speaker sets out to do (their goal; they word it themselves)
@keeper tavern_server
@keeper_situation Working a packed evening shift at the liveliest bar in town, a tray of mugs in hand.
@speaker_situation In the packed bar in town at night, at the counter where the server works; you came alone, and you are nervous around her.
warrior | Try to order an ale but stumble over the words because she is looking at you.
warrior | Try to compliment her braid and get the words wrong so it comes out awkward.
warrior | Apologise for the compliment, then apologise for apologising.
warrior | Admit you practised what to say to her on the walk over and forgot all of it.
warrior | Ask her, as a question to her, whether she minds if you just sit here and watch the band.
warrior | Tell her, blushing, that you came back tonight because she laughed at your joke last time.
warrior | Ask her, as a question to her, very awkwardly, whether she would maybe walk with you by the river sometime.
warrior | When she answers, thank her too many times and knock over your own mug.
